/-!
# Explicit zero-mode model for the augmented Candidate-A Hessian

This file replaces the anonymous finite-dimensional-kernel field of H12 by an
explicit finite type of physical zero modes and a linear equivalence from its
coordinate space to the genuine augmented Hessian kernel.

Once the modes are classified, only the coercive gap on their orthogonal
complement remains analytic.  The kernel dimension is exactly the number of
classified modes.
-/

namespace JanusFormal
namespace P0EFTJanusProgramPGlobalCandidateAActualZeroModeModel4D

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option maxHeartbeats 3800000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 1900000

noncomputable section

